                <pb facs="0306" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.05/159a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">De Billier</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-07T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>25. Department understands Judge Tuck has resigned.</p>
                <p>This Government desires appoint Judge Crabitès to Court of Appeals. Take up
                    matter orally immediately with proper authority and report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
